# Upstream: fixed in Linux 7.1 by 59eb73b98ae0 ("dax: Factor out dax_folio_reset_order() helper";
# union aliasing documented in 3fc3ebf40b5c), which clears folio->share = 0 unconditionally before
# the order-0 early return. Not backported to 6.18 stable; this carries the minimal 1-line fix
# without pulling in the 7.1 fsdev helper refactor.
dax: a folio's last entry going leaves it no share count

folio->share is a union with folio->index, and dax_folio_put left an
order 0 folio's as it was. A page that had an entry at a nonzero index
then looked shared: dax_associate_entry skipped dax_folio_init for a
shared PMD fault, whose entry named an order 0 folio (its WARN), and
vmf_insert_folio_pmd refused that folio, and the fault died of SIGBUS.
Found by cladefs's guest/sim; a filesystem saying a read's pages are
shared reaches it under window pressure (cladefs TASK-152).

diff --git a/fs/dax.c b/fs/dax.c
--- a/fs/dax.c
+++ b/fs/dax.c
@@ -392,6 +392,7 @@ static inline unsigned long dax_folio_put(struct folio *folio)
 		return ref;
 
 	folio->mapping = NULL;
+	folio->share = 0;
 	order = folio_order(folio);
 	if (!order)
 		return 0;
